# Nyia Keeper — egress firewall allowlist (Plan 280b)
#
# Active ONLY when `network_egress_policy=restrict-local` (see docs/NETWORK_EGRESS.md).
# Under that policy the assistant has FULL web egress but the local network is denied
# by default. Each line here punches a hole for ONE local destination.
#
# Format (exactly three fields):
#     <proto> <host> <port>
#   proto : tcp | udp
#   host  : a hostname or IPv4 literal (resolved when the firewall is compiled).
#           NO CIDRs, NO 0.0.0.0, NO wildcards.
#   port  : a single port 1..65535 (no ranges).
#
# Layering (merged, all applied): global ~/.config/nyiakeeper/config/network-allow.conf,
# then project .nyiakeeper/network-allow.conf, then .nyiakeeper/private/network-allow.conf.
#
# Copy to .nyiakeeper/network-allow.conf and edit. Changes take effect on next launch;
# the running session cannot modify the firewall (NET_ADMIN is dropped before it starts).

# Allow SSH to the test sidecar (akopso Plan 58) — runs tests over a forced-command shell.
tcp sidecar 2222

# NOTE: a LAN database is NOT listed, so it stays BLOCKED. To deny mysql you do nothing;
# to ALLOW it you would have to add a line like the following (left commented = denied):
#   tcp 192.168.1.50 3306      # <- only if you explicitly want the assistant to reach it
